":"Schock","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"shock (mental or medical condition)","termine_origine":"choc","catena":[{"codice":"fr","nome":"French","termine":"choc","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"en","nome":"English","termine":"shock","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"fro","nome":"Old French","termine":"choquer","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"frk","nome":"Frankish","termine":"*skokkōn","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmh","nome":"Middle High German","termine":"schoc","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"gmh","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Chiefly a borrowing (since 18th century), partly from French choc, partly from English shock, both derived from Old French choquer, from Frankish *skokkōn. There was also an uncommon native cognate, from Middle High German schoc (“wind gust”, rarely also “shock, thrust”), from Old High German scoc, "},{"parola":"Smoking","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"tuxedo, dinner jacket","termine_origine":"smoking","catena":[{"codice":"fr","nome":"French","termine":"smoking","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"en","nome":"English","termine":"","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"en","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from French smoking, and this a pseudo-anglicism, derived from an ellipsis of English smoking jacket."},{"parola":"Staatsmann","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"calco","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"perhaps","significato":"statesman","termine_origine":"homme d'État","catena":[{"codice":"fr","nome":"French","termine":"homme d'État","categoria":"calco"},{"codice":"en","nome":"English","termine":"statesman","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"en","ambiti":["diritto_politica"],"via":"","testo":"Late 17th century. From Staat (“state”) + -s- + Mann (“man”), calque of French homme d'État, perhaps after English statesman (late 16th century)."},{"parola":"Tagesordnung","pos":"noun","n_eti